\title{Biography}
\author{brentyorgey}

\import{base-macros}

\imgasset{walk-right.gif}

\p{I am an associate professor in (and current chair of) the [Department of Mathematics and Computer Science](https://hendrix-cs.github.io/) at [[hendrixcollege]] in Conway, Arkansas, USA. My research interests lie broadly within the fields of programming languages and discrete mathematics, with particular interests in functional programming languages, embedded domain-specific languages, category theory, combinatorics, and education.}

\p{I graduated from [[williamscollege]] in 2004, and obtained my PhD at the [[upenn]] in 2014, as part of the [Penn PL Club](http://www.cis.upenn.edu/~plclub/) and under the supervision of Dr. [[stephanieweirich]].}

\p{I live in Conway with my wife and three children (ages 14, 8, and 5). I enjoy [classical piano](00H7), [competitive programming](000F), [Go](https://senseis.xmp.net/), [Hanabi](https://hanabi.github.io/), ancient Greek and Hebrew, mountain biking, playing the occasional video game, and [reading](https://app.thestorygraph.com/profile/byorgey) (mostly science/speculative/historical fiction).}
